 "_verbs_as_data_note": "v2.1.0: the self-improvement verb inventory is GRAPH DATA -- Concept{name:<verb>, instruction_route:'self_improvement'} nodes seeded below -- and both rules match the predicate Mention resolving (intent's rule_mention_resolves_to_concept) to a route-carrying Concept, instead of an in-body verb list. Duplicate same-name Concepts from other seeds are harmless (the referent rule wires the Mention to every same-named Concept; the Exists finds the route-carrying one). EXTENSIBLE AT RUNTIME: teach(agent, 'Concept', {'name': 'recalibrate', 'instruction_route': 'self_improvement'}) extends coverage with no rule edit. NOTE both rules exclude ANY route-carrying instruction-verb Concept from counting as the grounded TARGET (instruction_route == null in the confidence Exists), so seeding the verb inventories does not fabricate confidence.",
 "description": "PHASE 3 (safe, bounded seam) of the graph-native conversation migration: the CONNECTION POINT between a chat instruction and the agent's self-improvement spine, established graph-natively and gated by the agent's OWN COMPREHENSION CONFIDENCE. v2.0.0 (creator directive: 'it should check its parsing, the context, and then mint something if confident, and ask for clarification otherwise -- graph-native, not Python'): a self-directed instruction (predicate improve/fix/correct/learn/change/update/adjust/refine) is handled by TWO mutually-exclusive rules that key on the agent's own referent resolution (seeds/intent.json wires Mention -refers_to-> Concept when a mention matches a held Concept's name, and Intent -about_concept-> it). CONFIDENCE is graph-native: did a CONTENT mention resolve to a held Concept -- one that is NEITHER the predicate verb NOR a second-person word (you/your/yourself/...)? (The verb and 'your' are themselves held Concepts and always resolve, so they are excluded as data literals in the where; what remains is a genuinely-grounded TARGET.) mint_self_improvement_concern_confident: a grounded target resolved -> the agent understood WHAT to work on -> mint Goal{kind:self_improvement} + SelfConcern{status:'noted'} (the human-gated seam into the existing, denylist+human-approval-gated self-improvement pipeline; NEVER 'pending', so nothing auto-runs) + a confident reply. ask_clarification_self_improvement: NO grounded target resolved -> the agent is NOT confident it understands the request -> it asks for clarification and mints NOTHING (no goal, no concern) -- exactly the 'ask otherwise' behaviour. Both use the agent -received-> m single-anchor match (the sd 'agent observed obs' pattern, never ['agent','is_a','Agent'] which over-fires) + the comprehended fixpoint guard. The decision (confident vs clarify) is the graph's, from the graph's own comprehension state -- no Python classifier.",
